```typescript
type ApiResult<T> = { ok: true; data: T } | { ok: false; error: string };
function handle(result: ApiResult<string>) {
  if (result.ok) {
    console.log(result.data);
  }
}
```
Why is `result.data` accessible only inside the `if (result.ok)` block?

```typescript
interface Point { x: number; y: number; }
function printPoint(p: Point) {}
printPoint({ x: 1, y: 2, z: 3 }); // ERROR

const coords = { x: 1, y: 2, z: 3 };
printPoint(coords); // OK
```
Both calls pass an identically-shaped value. Why does only the first one produce an error?
